Maintainer: Nicholas McKay <nick@nau.edu>
Description: Read, write, manipulate, and analyze Linked Paleo Data ('LiPD')
    files. 'LiPD' is a structured data standard for paleoclimate and
    paleoenvironmental data that keeps measurements together with their
    metadata, chronologies, and publication information. Provides tools to load
    single files or whole directories, validate their structure, flatten nested
    data into tidy time series for querying and filtering, and convert to and
    from the Neotoma Paleoecology Database. See McKay and Emile-Geay (2016)
    <doi:10.5194/cp-12-1093-2016> for a description of the 'LiPD' framework.
